  "id": "lexical-ambiguity",
  "term": "lexical ambiguity",
  "definition": "Lexical ambiguity is when a word has more than one possible meaning, such as a homonym, so the reader or listener must use context to decide which meaning fits. In language processing, this can involve activating both meanings or selecting the contextually appropriate one.",
